From: panel-diag <diag@local>
Subject: [r22i] drm/panel/boe-meizu20: profile-override knobs (H2 probe)

H1 verdict (knob stock, device): the exact downstream wake shape - no 0x07,
PPS after the full table, all LP - from a clean state still masks.  The
packet-level wake path is fully exonerated.

H2 probe: knob profile60/90/120/144 = real sleep + full replay at 120Hz
timing with a FOREIGN profile's 0x91 block and 0x2F selector.  If the mask
PATTERN changes with the forced profile, the sleep-out reload consumes the
commanded profile (H2 alive, fix = profile machinery); if identical, H2 is
dead too and the remaining ladder is H3 (stock-side DPU/DSI dumps) / S5
(XBL RE).  No multi-rate modes involved (r22g revert intact).

Diagnostic round - do not ship upstream as-is.
